 ### Added
 
-- `SessionStore.listFor(userId, options?)`, an optional store member that answers the summaries of a user's conversations — `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount` — most recent activity first, so a consumer can build a conversation list instead of only rejoining one. Nothing in the engine calls it yet: the store answers the list, and the route or frame that carries it to a client is still yours to write. `InMemorySessionStore` and `MongoSessionStore` both implement it; a store of your own may leave it out. A summary never carries a conversation's entries or its credentials. Page with `limit` (50 by default, 200 at most, and `0` answers nothing) and `before`, which takes the last summary you saw: the cursor carries both `updatedAt` and `sessionId`, so two conversations saved in the same millisecond cannot straddle a page boundary and go unlisted. See `docs/session-stores.md` § Listing a user's conversations.
+- **Conversation lists over the WebSocket.** A client sends `{type: 'list_sessions', limit?, before?}` on its authenticated socket and receives one `session_list` of the connecting user's own conversations, newest activity first: each row carries `sessionId`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO-8601 strings, and `entryCount`. There is no `userId` field to send — whose history is listed is read from the connection, and any `userId` a client does send is dropped. `limit` and `before` pass through to `SessionStore.listFor`, so a client pages with the same `before` cursor the store member takes; a malformed `limit` or `before` is refused with `INVALID_MESSAGE` before the store is asked. A store implementing no `listFor` answers an empty list; one whose `listFor` fails answers a single `error` frame with `SERVER_ERROR` and logs the failure without conversation content. A list is answered immediately, off the per-session lock, so it never queues behind a streaming answer, and it is only ever sent when asked for — the engine never pushes one.
+- `SessionStore.listFor(userId, options?)`, an optional store member that answers the summaries of a user's conversations — `sessionId`, `createdAt`, `updatedAt` and `entryCount` — most recent activity first, so a consumer can build a conversation list instead of only rejoining one. The engine now carries that list to a client itself, with the `list_sessions` frame above; an HTTP route over the same data is still yours to write. `InMemorySessionStore` and `MongoSessionStore` both implement it; a store of your own may leave it out. A summary never carries a conversation's entries or its credentials. Page with `limit` (50 by default, 200 at most, and `0` answers nothing) and `before`, which takes the last summary you saw: the cursor carries both `updatedAt` and `sessionId`, so two conversations saved in the same millisecond cannot straddle a page boundary and go unlisted. See `docs/session-stores.md` § Listing a user's conversations.
 
